85. Yuan Q, Chen X, Zhai J et al. Application of 3D modeling and fusion technology of medical image data in image teaching. BMC Med Educ 2021;21(1). [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 86. Cook DA. Randomized controlled trials and meta-analysis in medical education: what role do they play? Med Teach. 2012;34(6):468–73. doi: 10.3109/0142159X.2012.671978. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 87. Nourkami-Tutdibi N, Tutdibi E, Schmidt S, Zemlin M, Abdul-Khaliq H, Hofer M. Long-Term Knowledge Retention after peer-assisted abdominal Ultrasound Teaching: is PAL a successful model for Achieving Knowledge Retention? Ultraschall Med. 2020;41(1):36–43. doi: 10.1055/a-1034-7749. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 88. Feigin DS, Magid D, Smirniotopoulos JG, Carbognin SJ. Learning and retaining normal radiographic chest anatomy. Does preclinical exposure Improve Student performance? Acad Radiol. 2007;14(9):1137–42. doi: 10.1016/j.acra.2007.06.023. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 89. Doomernik DE, van Goor H, Kooloos JGM, Ten Broek RP. Longitudinal retention of anatomical knowledge in second-year medical students. Anat Sci Educ. 2017;10(3):242–8. doi: 10.1002/ase.1656. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 90. Ropovik I, Adamkovic M, Greger D. Neglect of publication bias compromises meta-analyses of educational research. PLoS ONE. 2021;16(6):e0252415. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0252415. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 91. Undergraduate Radiology RCR. Curriculum 2022. In: The Royal College of Radiologists; 2022. 92. Gadde JA, Ayoob A, Carrico CWT, Falcon S, Magid D, Miller-Thomas MM, Naeger D. AMSER National Medical Student Curriculum. 2020. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 93. Reddy S, Straus CM, McNulty NJ, et al. Development of the AMSER standardized examinations in radiology for medical students. Acad Radiol. 2015;22(1):130–4. doi: 10.1016/j.acra.2014.07.018. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials 12909_2023_4981_MOESM1_ESM.docx (15KB, docx) Supplementary Material 1: Data Points Extracted from Shortlisted Articles 12909_2023_4981_MOESM2_ESM.docx (13.5KB, docx) Supplementary Material 2: Definitions of Data Points 12909_2023_4981_MOESM3_ESM.tif (5.2MB, tif) Supplementary Material 3: Risk of Bias Assessment for Randomised Trials 12909_2023_4981_MOESM4_ESM.tif (2.3MB, tif) Supplementary Material 4: Risk of Bias Assessment for Non-Randomised Trials 12909_2023_4981_MOESM5_ESM.docx (81.4KB, docx) Supplementary Material 5: Topics and Modes of Assessment According to Student Seniority 12909_2023_4981_MOESM6_ESM.tif (2.6MB, tif) Supplementary Material 6: Active versus Passive Learning Subgroup Analysis 12909_2023_4981_MOESM7_ESM.tif (936.7KB, tif) Supplementary Material 7: eLearning versus No eLearning Subgroup Analysis 12909_2023_4981_MOESM8_ESM.tif (905.7KB, tif) Supplementary Material 8: Cross-Sectional Imaging versus No Cross-Sectional Imaging Subgroup Analysis 12909_2023_4981_MOESM9_ESM.tif (980.1KB, tif) Supplementary Material 9: Student Seniority Subgroup Analysis 12909_2023_4981_MOESM10_ESM.tif (864.4KB, tif) Supplementary Material 10: Imaging Professionals versus Non-Imaging Professionals as Teachers Subgroup Analysis 12909_2023_4981_MOESM11_ESM.tif (924.9KB, tif) Supplementary Material 11: Study Design Subgroup Analysis Data Availability Statement The datasets used and/or analysed during the current study are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request.',10,'2025-10-15 09:57:07','2025-10-15 09:57:07');
